  "summary": "Two parallel screws with intermeshing threads turn in opposite directions inside a figure-8 housing. External timing gears drive the second screw, so the threads never touch and can handle non-lubricating, viscous, abrasive or gas-laden liquids. In the double-flow arrangement shown, each screw has a left- and a right-handed section: liquid enters at both ends and is conveyed toward the centre outlet, balancing axial thrust. Used for crude oil, bitumen, multiphase production fluids, polymers and food products.",
